column9:
Thanks for the reply. I don't argue that it's not to spec, just that it seems not useful/a bit surprising.<p>Some other languages (e.g. perl and I think also java) choose to make the loop var an alias, rather than a copy, to allow mutation:<p><pre><code>    for my $item (@items) {
        $item->frob; # Can happily mutate the item
    }
</code></pre>
will work as it reads.
